---
import { linkInstagramMentions } from "../../utils/instagramMentions";
import ArtworkMeta from "../../components/art/ArtworkMeta.astro";

const metaVenue = linkInstagramMentions("@aapex_lab");
const metaOrganised = linkInstagramMentions("@sophiologin");
---

<div class="mt-4 max-w-3xl">
  <ArtworkMeta fields={[
    { label: "Year", value: "2026" },
    { label: "First played", value: "20 September 2026" },
    { label: "Venue", value: metaVenue, html: true },
    { label: "Organised by", value: metaOrganised, html: true },
    { label: "Software", value: "SuperCollider" },
  ]} />

  <p class="mb-4">
    A sequencer that treats the sample folder as a database. You type words: kick, impact, glitch, loop
    and so on, then the rows fill with whatever matches.
  </p>

  <p class="mb-4">
    I gave up some control over the rhythm. Each row runs its own algorithm, so nothing lines up for long.
  </p>

  <p class="mb-4">
    The idea of putting all the sound in RAM is borrowed from <a href="https://renickbell.net" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Renick Bell</a>'s
    <a href="https://github.com/renickbell/konduktiva" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Konduktiva</a>.
    The whole program is written in SuperCollider.
  </p>

  <div class="art-media-grid">
    <figure class="art-media-full">
      <video controls preload="metadata" poster="/images/query/query-cover.jpg">
        <source src="/video/query.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
      <figcaption class="mt-2 text-sm opacity-70">Screen recording — typing a query, rows filling with matching samples</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</div>
